target_text:
// Opaque pointers to the page's K/V accessors. Templated page
// type is erased behind lambdas that populate() invokes.
// k_head_fn(slot, kv_head, scratch) -> bf16* to this token's K row.
// v_head_fn(slot, kv_head, scratch) -> bf16* to this token's V row.
// A row is HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE bf16 values in dimension order. The pointer is
// into the page when the page stores the row contiguously, else into the
// caller-owned, 64-byte-aligned scratch where the callback rebuilt the row.
// The row is spread for K under TRON_K_VNNI (Note [K VNNI storage],
// kv_cache.hpp) and for V always (Note [VNNI Packed V layout], v_vnni.hpp).

body:
**[comments] Rule 4, comment lines that map to no code line: shorten**

The 17-line comment sits above two std::function declarations, and its lines 67-77 (the K VNNI line geometry, the V pair interleave, and why both are the AMX B-operand order) map to no line of gof.hpp: they restate Note [K VNNI storage] (kv_cache.hpp:653-661, 672-673), the k_vnni.hpp header (lines 13-17, 29-30) and Note [VNNI Packed V layout] (v_vnni.hpp:33-44). The contract facts that the types do not carry (row size and order, page-or-scratch aliasing of the returned pointer, scratch ownership and 64-byte alignment) stay as three lines plus one pointer line to the two Notes. Lines 59-60 are unchanged context and are repeated verbatim in the proposed text.

